- whether the supplied tests are adequate verifiers of the real CLI;
- whether the plan agrees with the fixed commands;
- the causal link from the historical baseline failure (result 6514754a) to the correction;
- current command evidence on the corrected CLI: exit 0, exact stdout, at least two passes, zero failures.
Unmet and indeterminate criteria must be preserved.

Write `specification/project-conformance.md` for a minimal CLI Hello World software-build traversal. It must state:
- the Intent;
- the Product boundary: a Node CLI with no package or network dependency;
- source-grounded requirements;
- completion criteria.

The source surface is `generated/hello-world.mjs`. The execution proof runs the CLI and observes stdout of exactly `Hello, world!\n` with exit 0. Completion also requires both supplied component and UAT tests to execute the real CLI, with at least two passes and zero failures, backed by truthful admitted execution evidence rather than a prewritten report. Write no source, tests, package files or execution plans.

